course: dictionary
lesson: 6855
title: The ovary
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ovary is a body part that makes or holds eggs. In female animals and people, an ovary makes egg cells. In a flower, the ovary is the part at the bottom that holds the seeds before they grow.
explain: Plants and animals use the word in different ways, but the idea is the same: the ovary is where new life starts. «After fertilisation the ovules become seeds and the flower's ovary, the swollen bottom part of the pistil, grows into a fruit.» So the ovary is swollen, which means it gets bigger.
explain: Use the context to check the meaning. The sentence says the ovary grows into a fruit. Fruit is something that grows from a flower, so the ovary must be the part that becomes the fruit.
fact: An ovary is one of the organs that make egg cells in female animals and people.
fact: In a flower, the ovary is at the base and holds the seeds before they grow.
fact: After pollination, the ovary grows into a fruit.
fact: Women have two ovaries.
fact: Fertilisation is what happens before the ovules become seeds.
exercise: «After fertilisation the ovules become seeds and the flower's ovary grows into a fruit.» What does the ovary grow into? | A petal | *A fruit | A root | A leaf
exercise: Which part of a flower holds the seeds before they grow? | Stamen | Stigma | Petal | *Ovary
exercise: In female animals and people, what does an ovary make? | Petals | Pollen | *Egg cells | Fruit
test: In a flower, where is the ovary found? | At the top, above the petals | In the leaves | In the roots | *At the base, at the bottom
test: How many ovaries do most women have? | One | *Two | Three | Four
exam: What does the ovary become after pollination in a flower? | A petal | A root | A stamen | *A fruit
